## Working here

| To | Run |
|---|---|
| Start a decision record: the next number, the template, and its row in the index | `cargo xtask decision new "<title>" [--status TEXT] [--dry-run]` |
| Edit while `xtask` itself does not build (in the middle of a change to it) | `./x replace …` or `./x links`: it builds `xtask` first and, when that fails, runs the last binary that ran a command to its end, kept in `target/xtask-last-good/` (`xtask.exe` on Windows, run by its path). It says how old it is and which commit it came from, and offers only `replace` and `links` |
| Write the open items' index from the items' files, after adding, settling or changing an item, and after a rebase (git merges the index line by line and never stops on it; `rules` fails until it is written again) | `cargo xtask outstanding` (`--check` only compares) |

`./x <command>` is the same as `cargo xtask <command>`.
